WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:06.239
For decades, scientists have been working on materials
that can change shape.

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.249
Whether it's bending, contracting, or wriggling along,

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:17.368
these kinds of smart materials could be useful for robotics, engineering and medicine.

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:22.889
So far, many of these materials transform relatively slowly.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.240
Sometimes they need to be connected to a controller with wires or tubes,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:32.660
or they have a limited range of movements.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:39.300
Now scientists have developed a flexible smart material that is remotely activated

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.820
can move in multiple ways,

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.117
and can transform quickly,

00:00:44.117 --> 00:00:47.249
changing its shape completely in less than a second.

00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:58.529
This material can be 3D printed, and scientists use magnets to change its shape.

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:11.480
The technique uses a soft silicon rubber embedded with tiny particles of iron.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:14.750
A magnetic field is used to magnetise the substance

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:19.970
creating a magnetic material that can be printed into any shape

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:24.380
And, the direction of the magnetic field can be changed during printing.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.579
The result is a material with a non-uniform polarity

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:34.759
meaning each part of the structure can respond differently to a magnetic charge.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.250
Scientists added a red filter to film the movements.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:48.259
The system is so precise that researchers can program a computer model to move in a certain way

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.940
print it out,

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:55.560
and the same movement can be replicated exactly in the physical structure.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:03.300
The team have already made shapes that can contract,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.400
Deform,

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:10.399
Stop a ball,

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.780
Catch a ball,

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.400
and even jump.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.900
But there are countless more possibilities

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:26.720
If it can be modelled,

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:29.380
it can be made.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:38.680
Because the magnetic field is applied remotely, these materials can be used in small, inaccessible places.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:45.480
In medicine this could be useful inside the body for delivering drugs or in surgery

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:53.740
Or in robotics, the complex shape changes could give soft robots flexible appendages.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:58.160
In fact, along with existing smart materials,

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:04.480
this speedy shape-changing technology has numerous potential uses in a range of industries

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:08.260
all with just the flip of a magnetic switch.

